              "id": "CVE-2019-14900",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2019-14900: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2019-14900?s=github&n=hibernate-core&ns=org.hibernate&t=maven&vr=%3C5.3.18",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in Hibernate ORM in versions before 5.3.18, 5.4.18 and 5.5.0.Beta1. A SQL injection in the implementation of the JPA Criteria API can permit unsanitized literals when a literal is used in the SELECT or GROUP BY parts of the query. This flaw could allow an attacker to access unauthorized information or possibly conduct further attacks.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in Hibernate ORM in versions before 5.3.18, 5.4.18 and 5.5.0.Beta1. A SQL injection in the implementation of the JPA Criteria API can permit unsanitized literals when a literal is used in the SELECT or GROUP BY parts of the query. This flaw could allow an attacker to access unauthorized information or possibly conduct further attacks.\n\n|                                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:maven/org.hibernate/hibernate-core@3.6.10.Final  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <5.3.18                                              |\n|Fixed version                                                                  5.3.18                                               |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                                                       |\n"
              },
